==Trivia==
*Most of the stages' names are related to their contents:
**The "Disaster" in [[Disaster Cycle]] may be a hint towards the stage having [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angels]] that was lost in translation. It was translated from 天変地異 ''tenpenchii'', an idiom that refers to a catastrophic natural disaster, but contains 天, a kanji meaning heaven/sky.
**[[Three Evil Brothers]] has three different enemies of the same species: [[Kory]], [[Berserkory]] and [[Koronium]].
**[[Pulled Punch Bout]] is named after "pulling punches", an idiom meaning "to hold back", as in restraining oneself when punching or wording a phrase delicately when speaking to avoid giving offense or inciting anger. Pulling punches is indeed encouraged in this stage, as doing so will allow you to fight the bosses one at a time rather than simultaneously.
**[[Border Between Worlds]] refers to the border between the world of the living and the world after death, hence the [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]]; its Japanese name can be literally translated as "Border Between This World and That World", but あの世 ''ano yo'' ("that world") is a euphemism for the world after death.
**[[Hall of the Four Kings]] has four threats: [[Elder Sloth]], [[St. Dober]], [[M. Ost]] and [[Assassin Bear]]. Although this stage's name is likely a reference to the [[wikipedia:Hall of Four Heavenly Kings|Hall of Four Heavenly Kings]], only St. Dober is heavenly.
*This is the first sub-chapter to have a difficulty rating of ★11.

